<title>USA: Golf-Elkington holds off Tiger to hold top spot on money list.</title>
<headline>Golf-Elkington holds off Tiger to hold top spot on money list.</headline>
<dateline>PONTE VEDRA BEACH, Florida 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Steve Elkington has held on to top spot on the U.S. PGA Tour money winners list but faces a growing challenge from Masters champion Tiger Woods.</p>
<p>Elkington was the first player on tour to pass the one million dollar mark this season.</p>
<p>Fellow Australian Stuart Appleby lies seventh on the list. Compatriot and world number one Greg Norman, who missed the cut at Augusta last weekend, does not make the top 20.</p>
<p>Leading players (U.S. unless stated):</p>
<p>  1. Steve Elkington (Australia)   1,059,070</p>
<p>  2. Tiger Woods			   966,350</p>
<p>  3. Mark O'Meara			  850,943</p>
<p>  4. Jesper Parnevik (Sweden)	  632,510</p>
<p>  5. Scott Hoch			    596,315</p>
<p>  6. Paul Stankowski		     580,298</p>
<p>  7. Stuart Appleby (Australia)	550,921</p>
<p>  8. Steve Jones			   504,290</p>
<p>  9. Brad Faxon			    481,220</p>
<p> 10. Tommy Tolles			  452,659</p>
<p> 11. Craig Stadler			 447,676</p>
<p> 12. Tom Lehman			    418,821</p>
<p> 13. Phil Mickelson			400,150</p>
<p> 14. John Cook			     361,813</p>
<p> 15. Tom Kite				360,683</p>
<p> 16. Nick Price (South Africa)	 347,440</p>
<p> 17. Mark Calcavecchia		   343,861</p>
<p> 18. Michael Bradley		     341,086</p>
<p> 19. David Duval			   331,485</p>
<p> 20. Jeff Sluman			   326,406</p>
